  "title": "wslua: We don't need to register conversation data with the proto",
  "description": "The conversation data is file scoped, and there's already a callback\nto free all the Lua-related information when the file scope leaves.\nThere's no need to register it to the protocols (which have different\nmemory scope) or free it when deregistering the protocols (which can\nhappen outside of file scope and thus lead to a heap-use-after-free.)\n\nFixup dab146cba09fec377a9dcc87ee6a8e14288e9b5d",
